<title>BRAZIL: Bradesco to post record profit - report.</title>
<headline>Bradesco to post record profit - report.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bradesco, Brazil's largest retail bank, is expected to report a record profit in the order of 800 million reais ($770 million) for 1996, Veja newsweekly reported on Monday.</p>
<p>Veja said Bradesco's unprecedented results would be the highest ever reported by a private Brazilian company. The newspaper did not say when the results would be announced.</p>
<p>Veja dedicated its cover story this week to Lazaro Brandao, the low profile Bradesco president.</p>
<p>((-- Adrian Dickson, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 248 5410))</p>
